WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.437
On this slide, we are focusing on evaluate predictions.

00:00:03.437 --> 00:00:08.047
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.047 --> 00:00:13.682
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:13.682 --> 00:00:21.182
Accuracy summarizes the fraction of correct predictions, while a confusion matrix shows which classes were

00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:24.612
confused. Before clicking Run, predict the structure of the output.

00:00:24.612 --> 00:00:31.517
After it runs, identify the features, target, split, prediction, or evaluation result involved.

00:00:31.517 --> 00:00:36.757
Change one input carefully and explain why the result did or did not change.

00:00:36.757 --> 00:00:42.517
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:47.936
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
